  {
   "identifier": "p-text",
   "id": "doc-1e6gu5akk0",
   "content": {
    "text": "<em>Listen and subscribe to the podcast «NZZ Akzent» on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/show/4uoTZbK8rBcVAzAk5f7tIr?si=Qog1qTM4ROaG-fzLBxIgNA\">Spotify,</a> <a href=\"https://podcasts.apple.com/ch/podcast/nzz-akzent/id1506761994\">Apple Podcasts,</a> or <a href=\"https://castbox.fm/channel/NZZ-Akzent-id2982237\">Castbox.</a></em><a href=\"https://podcasts.apple.com/ch/podcast/nzz-corona-podcast/id1506761994\"></a>"
   },
   "data": {},
   "paidContent": true,
   "prevElement": "barrier",
   "nextElement": "subtitle"
  },
  {
   "identifier": "subtitle",
   "id": "doc-1e31r87h90",
   "content": {
    "title": "In this podcast episode",
    "id": "subtitle-in-dieser-podcast-episode"
   },
   "contentTable": false,
   "paidContent": true,
   "prevElement": "p-text",
   "nextElement": "p-text"
  },
  {
   "identifier": "p-text",
   "id": "doc-1jogcllb10",
   "content": {
    "text": "The sea roars, the sun shines, people stroll along the promenade with an ice cream or drink coffee in a trendy cafe. Walking through the streets of Odesa, one almost feels as if on vacation on the Riviera. But the idyll is deceptive. As soon as night falls, sirens wail, Russian drones fly in over the Black Sea, and detonations echo through the historic alleyways."
   },
   "paidContent": true,
   "prevElement": "subtitle",
   "nextElement": "p-text"
  },
  {
   "identifier": "p-text",
   "id": "doc-1k0prr0a30",
   "content": {
    "text": "Far from the front line, a decisive battle is being fought here. It is about nothing less than the economic survival of Ukraine. The country handles its export trade through the ports around Odesa. Agricultural products are shipped from here, and their revenues are indispensable for the state budget and for global markets."
   },
   "paidContent": true,
   "prevElement": "p-text",
   "nextElement": "p-text"
  },
  {
   "identifier": "p-text",
   "id": "doc-1k0ps8ipc0",
   "content": {
    "text": "For a long time, Ukraine was able to secure exports because it succeeded in pushing back the Russian fleet. But now, Russia has intensified its attacks around Odesa, and the situation has changed dramatically."
   },
   "paidContent": true,
   "prevElement": "p-text",
   "nextElement": "p-text"
  },
  {
   "identifier": "p-text",
   "id": "doc-1k0hokcr91",
   "content": {
    "text": "Reporter Jonas Roth traveled to Odesa to get a picture of the situation. In the «NZZ Akzent» podcast, he describes how the city is trying to defend itself against Russia and why Odesa continues to serve as an oasis for the entire country."
   },
   "paidContent": true,
   "prevElement": "p-text",
   "nextElement": "p-text"
  },
  {
   "identifier": "p-text",
   "id": "doc-1icgi7ejd1",
   "content": {
    "text": "<em>All episodes of «NZZ Akzent» can be found in <a href=\"http://www.nzz.ch/podcast/akzent\">this overview</a>.</em>"
   },
   "paidContent": true,
